      "side": 1,
      "message": "These fds end up being unused except for the purpose of getting a `file` structure for a wrap. What I did instead was that I implemented a function that is only exposed to this test and it takes in a dmabuf, and allocates the associated structures (i.e. context, content). It supports a NULL argument which creates an empty wrap. The return type is a `struct file *` that you can then use with the wrapfd kernel API.\n\nI\u0027ve implemented it here: https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/kernel/common/+/4412986/2/drivers/android/wrapfd/wrap.rs",
